# Example TLS termination at Nginx (operator-owned certificates).
# Copy patterns into the main server block or a separate listen 443 server.
#
# Assumptions for this app:
# - Browser Origin must match ALLOWED_ORIGINS exactly (e.g. https://learn.example.com).
# - Go backend listens on internal HTTP (:8080); TLS terminates here (or upstream LB).
# - X-Forwarded-* may be set for logs; the Go app does not use them for origin allowlisting.
